    "focus": [],
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Given an unsorted array arr[] of size n, containing elements from the range 1 to n, it is known that one number in this range is missing, and another number occurs twice in the array, find both the duplicate number and the missing number."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "language": "javascript",
        "text": "Examples:\n\nInput: arr[] = [2, 2]\nOutput: [2, 1]\nExplanation: Repeating number is 2 and the missing number is 1.\nInput: arr[] = [1, 3, 3] \nOutput: [3, 2]\nExplanation: Repeating number is 3 and the missing number is 2.\nInput: arr[] = [4, 3, 6, 2, 1, 1]\nOutput: [1, 5]\nExplanation: Repeating number is 1 and the missing number is 5."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Intution"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Better Approach -1"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "step-1 . create a Hash Array of n+1 size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "step-2. run a loop from 0 to n-1 and increase hash[arr[i]] by 1"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "step-3. take two variable repeating and missing"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "step4. Run a loop again from 1 till n and if hash[arr[i]]==2 then repeating =i and if hash[arr[i]]==0 then missing =i"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "step5. add both variable in arraylist"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Solution"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "text": "class Solution {\n    ArrayList<Integer> findTwoElement(int arr[]) {\n        // code here\n        int n=arr.length;\n        //create a hash array \n        int [] hash=new int[n+1];\n        Arrays.fill(hash,0);\n        int repeating=-1;\n        int missing=-1;\n        //Aarraylist to store ans\n        ArrayList<Integer> ans=new ArrayList<>();\n        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){\n            hash[arr[i]]++;\n        }\n        for(int i=1;i<hash.length;i++){\n            if(hash[i]==2) repeating=i;\n            else if(hash[i]==0) missing=i;\n            if(missing!=-1 && repeating!=-1) break;\n        }\n        ans.add(repeating);\n        ans.add(missing);\n        return ans;\n    }\n}"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Optimal  Appraoch- 1"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "This is Math approach where we will create two equation and solve them and we get missing and repeating number."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Intution"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-1. Get the sum from 1 to n and store in x"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-2. Get the sum of each element of array and store in y"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-3. Now get the sum of square from 1 to n"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-4. Get the sum of square of each element of array"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-5. Now get val1=x-y and val2=x2-y2"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Step-6. Solve the equation and get x and y"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "language": "java",
        "text": "class Solution {\n    ArrayList<Integer> findTwoElement(int arr[]) {\n        // code here\n        ArrayList<Integer> ans=new ArrayList<>();\n        int  n=arr.length;\n        long x=0;\n        long x2=0;\n        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){\n            x+=arr[i];\n            x2+=((long)arr[i]*arr[i]);\n        }\n        long y=((long)n*(n+1))/2;\n        long y2=((long)n*(n+1)*(2*n+1))/6;\n        \n        long val1=x-y;\n        long val2=x2-y2;\n        val2=val2/val1;\n        int r = (int) ((val1 + val2) / 2);\n        int m = (int) (r - val1);\n\n        \n        ans.add(r);\n        ans.add(m);\n        return ans;\n    }\n}"
      }
    ],
